## 1 Didier Blanchet

### Microsimulating French pension prospects: the Destinie model

The Destinie model is a dynamic microsimulation model whose construction started in the early 1990s. Its main purpose is the long run projection of pensions. It has been used for analyzing the impact of reforms that have taken place in France since 1993. This paper explains the context that led to the construction of its first version, the main choices decided upon for this version and its major applications. We present the lessons drawn from these applications and we examine improvements introduced by the new version of the model, available since 2011. 


